Echo and lung ultrasound accreditation, from the Salford Critical Care portal — 18 Sept.

Ali: "link into my critcareultrasound site and in the search box show who is echo and lung US
accredted as a skill" · "it msut only show accredited not in trainign".

Two FIND skills, exactly like PICC — searchable from Who can…, read by nothing in the
allocator, and they never move anybody between pods. Icons are a heart and a pair of lungs,
coloured from the portal's own module accents so the two systems agree at a glance.

ONLY ACCREDITED, NEVER IN TRAINING. The source is a view created for this and nothing else,
public.v_accredited_for_rota, which reads the portal's Accreditation table alone. TrainingCycle
and Competency — where somebody part-way through lives — are not in it and are never queried.
Leavers are excluded at source: that is what takes 36 rows down to 20 people (16 echo, 4 lung).

A BLANK IS NOT A NO. The portal knows ~30 people and the unit has ~130, so the sync only ever
GRANTS and never revokes. Removing an accreditation stays a deliberate human act on the Staff
page, because the portal not mentioning somebody is not evidence about them.

NAMES DO NOT MATCH AND THE SYNC DOES NOT GUESS. The portal says "Dong Lin", the rota says
"Lin Dong"; "Dave Garwood" against "David Garwood". Matching is exact, then the same words in
any order, and nothing looser — a near-spelling match would risk granting a clinical skill to
the wrong person. Anything unmatched is printed for a human. Two people of one name are left
alone. Runs report-only unless given --apply.

  index.html                                   FLAGS, icons, colours, SK_COLS, FIND_KEYS
  docs/CCU Pod Allocator/allocate-pull/ultrasound_sync.py   new
  (and a read-only view in the ultrasound Supabase — additive, no data changed)

Tests: render 310 passed / 1 failed (pre-existing, unrelated) · strength 135/0 · locum probe
27/0. Six new assertions, including that neither skill is a pod rule or a phone rule.

STILL TO DO: this is the resident board, where Who can… already exists. Cover has no search
yet — that is the next piece, and the DPIA needs this flow adding to Section 4 of both
assessments before it is switched on.
